GIT - global information transfer
definition of git: used to push or pull the project source code into the git platform
definition of github: a git's built-in platform that is used to store the project folders and can collaborate with project developers / terminal

git config user.name "user_name"
git config user.email "user_email" 

-- used to config the users details in git configuration

git init - initialization of git





ls - list contents/files of folder
ls -al -list hidden contents of folder
touch file_name - used to create file

vi file_name or vim file_name || linux command to enter or edit the file
then to insert new content:
i for insert, so select i which shows Insert on the terminal
then enter the content
then click 'esc' to exit the entering mode

:wq - to save the file
cat - to show the content in that file
ex: cat file_name
shows the list of content




**************** order *****************
touch dev1

--creates a file with dev1 as file_name

cat dev1

-- used to show the data or information present in the dev1 file

vi dev1 || vim dev1 

-- takes to other platform like unix that can edit the platform

then press 'i' to enter Insert Mode, and enter the text you needed

first line of terminal mode or git bash terminal mode entering or editing file

-- after entering the data or information or content, press
-- 'ESC' button to exit the entering or editing mode

:wq 

-- this is used to save the edited file dev1
-- then it returns back to the git bash terminal

cat dev1

-- shows the content present in the dev1 file_name which is
-- "first line of terminal mode or git bash terminal mode entering or editing file"

-- this is the overall order to edit the folder or file


master - is the branch

git status

--  shows the status of the file / folder

git add . || git add dev1

-- to add all files or folders, we use '.' || to add only specific files or folders, we use 'git add file_name or folder_name

git commit -m "Message"

-- used to add a message (-m) what we edited or changed the file/folder
